# Calls to the gateway (port 3000), the only public entry point.
# Paste a fresh Auth0 access token (the long eyJ… string). Don't commit a real one.
# /me needs a token from a logged-in person: log in through the app and copy it,
# or use `auth0 test token`. Tokens from the API's Test tab are machine tokens → 403 on /me.
@token = PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN

### Public endpoint, no token needed
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### Catalog (public): categories
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/categories

### Catalog: all services, or one category's
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/services?category=canalizacao

### Catalog: one service page
GET http://localhost:3000/catalog/services/desentupimento-lavatorio-sanita

### No token → 401
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami

### Any valid token → 200 with its claims
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tampered token → 401
GET http://localhost:3000/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}x

### My profile → 404 until I register, then 200 (403 with a machine token)
GET http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Register my profile → 201 (auth0Id comes from the token, not the body)
POST http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao@example.com", "name": "João" }

### Register again → 409 from users-service, passed through by the gateway
POST http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao@example.com" }

### Change my name / phone → 200 (email can't be changed here: it belongs to Auth0)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "João Pedro", "phone": "+351912345678" }

### Stop users-service, then → 503
GET http://localhost:3000/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
